{
  "_readme": [
    "Hand-maintained company tiers for the internship tab's prestige signal.",
    "",
    "WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Prestige was originally derived only from collection data, on the",
    "principle that a derived signal beats a list somebody has to keep up to date. Measured on",
    "a real corpus that turned out not to work: Google had 1 posting from 1 source while Tesla",
    "had 78 and TikTok 114, so every derived signal available ranked volume, not quality. Pay",
    "would have been the honest proxy and exactly 1 company of 455 had a pay figure. The data",
    "does not contain the signal, so it is stated here instead of invented.",
    "",
    "Derived scoring still runs for every company NOT listed here, so this file does not have",
    "to be exhaustive to be useful. Adding a company moves it into the curated band; leaving",
    "one out just means it is ranked on evidence.",
    "",
    "`keys` are normalized company keys as produced by `normalize::company_key` (lowercase,",
    "legal suffixes stripped). Several per company on purpose: this doubles as the alias table",
    "that `dedup` deliberately does not have. A real example from live data — `palantir` and",
    "`palantir technologies` arrived as two separate companies, and `docs/INTERNSHIP_SCRAPING",
    ".md` C notes that parent/subsidiary pairs like Google/Alphabet are a knowledge problem",
    "with no algorithmic fix.",
    "",
    "TIERS ARE A JUDGEMENT, NOT A FACT. They are one person's ordering of desirability and",
    "will not match anyone else's. Edit freely — this is data, and nothing in the code depends",
    "on any particular company being present or on the tier count."
  ],
